Call For Tutorials

https://popl27.sigplan.org/track/POPL-2027-tutorials#Call-For-Tutorials

The 54th ACM SIGPLAN Symposium on Principles of Programming Languages
(POPL 2027) will be held in Mexico City, Mexico.

POPL provides a forum for the discussion of fundamental principles and
important innovations in the design, definition, analysis,
transformation, implementation and verification of programming
languages, programming systems, and programming abstractions.

Tutorials for POPL 2027 are solicited on any topic relevant to the
POPL community. We particularly encourage submissions of introductory
tutorials that make the research presented at POPL more accessible to
the participants.

Tutorials will be held from January 9th (afternoon) to the 11th. The
expected length of a tutorial is either 1.5 or 3 hours, including
questions and discussion (Q&A).

Submission details

- Deadline for submission: October 9, 2026
- Notification of acceptance: October 23, 2026

A tutorial proposal should provide the following information:

- Tutorial title
- Presenter(s), affiliation(s), and contact information
- Length (1.5 hour or 3 hours)
- 1-3 page description (for evaluation). This should include the
    objectives, topics to be covered, presentation approach, target
    audience, prerequisite knowledge, and if the tutorial was
    previously held, the location (i.e. which conference), date, and
    number of attendees if available.
- 1-2 paragraph abstract suitable for tutorial publicity.
- 1-paragraph biography suitable for tutorial publicity.

Proposals must be submitted by email to Aws Albarghouthi
(aws@cs.wisc.edu) and Alan Schmitt (alan.schmitt@inria.fr) with the
subject line =E2=80=9CPOPL 2027 Tutorial Proposal: [tutorial name]=E2=80=9D=
. The
proposal should be attached as a PDF, docx, or txt file.

Further information

Any questions regarding POPL 2027 tutorials should be
addressed to the workshops chairs, Aws Albarghouthi (aws@cs.wisc.edu)
and Alan Schmitt (alan.schmitt@inria.fr).

